{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q425176","formula":"CNNaS","hill":"CNNaS","elements":["C","N","Na","S"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"N":1.0,"S":1.0,"Na":1.0},"names":{"en":"Sodium thiocyanate","ru":"Тиоцианат натрия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sodium thiocyanate (sometimes called sodium sulphocyanide) is the chemical compound with the formula NaSCN. This colorless deliquescent salt is one of the main sources of the thiocyanate anion. As such, it is used as a precursor for the synthesis of pharmaceuticals and other specialty chemicals. Thiocyanate salts are typically prepared by the reaction of cyanide with elemental sulfur: 8 NaCN + S8 → 8 NaSCN Sodium thiocyanate crystallizes in an orthorhombic cell.","ru":"Тиоцианат натрия NaSCN (техническое название — роданистый натрий) — неорганическое вещество, натриевая соль роданистоводородной кислоты. Бесцветные ромбические гигроскопичные кристаллы, хорошо растворимые в воде, растворимые в ацетоне, метаноле, этаноле. Из воды ниже 30,4 °С кристаллизуется в виде дигидрата, выше — в виде безводной соли."},"fame":27,"pubchemCid":516871,"mass":81.07,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(#N)[S-].[Na+]","inchikey":"VGTPCRGMBIAPIM-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"sodium thiocyanate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-6633","atoms":16,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[13.61,0.0,0.0],[0.0,4.121,0.0],[0.0,0.0,5.681]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":12.195,"y":1.03,"z":3.223,"el":"Na"},{"x":8.219,"y":3.091,"z":0.382,"el":"Na"},{"x":1.414,"y":3.091,"z":2.458,"el":"Na"},{"x":5.391,"y":1.03,"z":5.299,"el":"Na"},{"x":1.585,"y":1.03,"z":4.937,"el":"C"},{"x":5.22,"y":3.091,"z":2.097,"el":"C"},{"x":8.39,"y":1.03,"z":3.584,"el":"C"},{"x":12.025,"y":3.091,"z":0.743,"el":"C"},{"x":2.511,"y":1.03,"z":0.598,"el":"S"},{"x":11.099,"y":3.091,"z":5.083,"el":"S"},{"x":4.294,"y":3.091,"z":